course: dictionary
lesson: 59
title: Acetic and vinegar
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scientists use special words for things they test. Acetic is one of them. You do not need to know it before you read, because the words around it give you clues. «Vinegar is water with acetic acid in it, made by bacteria from wine or cider.» The word acid tells you that acetic is describing a type of acid.
explain: Acetic means to do with vinegar or acetic acid. Acetic acid is the weak acid that gives vinegar its sour taste and sharp smell. So when you see acetic, think vinegar. Swap in your meaning: «Vinegar is water with vinegar's weak acid in it» still makes sense, so you have the right idea.
explain: In science lessons, you may test acids. When vinegar meets bicarbonate of soda, the mixture fizzes. The acetic acid in the vinegar is part of the reaction. Look for the clue words: acid, sour, sharp smell, and vinegar.
fact: Acetic is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as acid.
fact: Acetic acid is the weak acid that gives vinegar its sour taste and sharp smell.
fact: «Acetic» means to do with vinegar or acetic acid.
fact: «Vinegar is water with acetic acid in it, made by bacteria from wine or cider.»
fact: Context clues, like the word acid nearby, can help you work out a science word.
exercise: «Vinegar is water with acetic acid in it, made by bacteria from wine or cider.» What does acetic mean here? | *To do with vinegar and its acid | To do with cold water | To do with wine bottles | To do with bacteria only
exercise: What gives vinegar its sour taste and sharp smell? | Cider | Bicarbonate of soda | Water | *Acetic acid
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Vinegar is water with acetic acid in it» that describes the acid. | vinegar | water | with | *acetic
test: In a science test, vinegar fizzes when mixed with bicarbonate of soda. Which word describes the weak acid in vinegar? | *Acetic | Sweet | Salty | Cold
test: What does acetic mean? | To do with the sea | A type of bacteria | *To do with vinegar or acetic acid | Made of metal
exam: Which is the best meaning of acetic acid? | *The weak acid that gives vinegar its sour taste and sharp smell | A sweet liquid made from fruit | A gas that makes bread rise | A strong acid that is found in rocks
